      <section class="site-shell section" data-reveal="up">
        <div class="app-showcase">
          <img src="{{ asset('assets/img/app-preview.svg') }}" alt="Sorty app preview showing scan and repair recommendation">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
            <h2 class="headline" style="font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5.8rem);">Simple decisions for circular textiles.</h2>
            <div class="steps">
              <div class="step">
                <div>
                  <h3>Take a photo</h3>
                  <p>Users take a photo of a garment and answer a short set of questions about its condition.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <div>
                  <h3>Get a recommendation</h3>
                  <p>The app analyzes the item and recommends the most appropriate pathway, such as resale, consignment, repair, donation, or recycling.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="step">
                <div>
                  <h3>Find a nearby place</h3>
                  <p>Sorty displays a map of nearby locations where the item can be taken, helping garments stay in use longer.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="site-shell section" data-reveal="up">
        <div class="grid two" data-reveal-group>
          <article class="card" data-reveal-item>
            <span class="eyebrow">Why it exists</span>
            <h3>Textile waste is one of the fastest-growing waste streams globally.</h3>
            <p>Most people do not know what to do with unwanted clothing, and even when clothing is donated, systems are overwhelmed. It is estimated that up to 70% of donated garments are never resold, leading to export, downcycling, or disposal.</p>
            <p class="source-link">Source: <a href="https://www.epa.gov/facts-and-figures-about-materials-waste-and-recycling/textiles-material-specific-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. EPA Textiles Material-Specific Data</a>; corroborated by secondary market research on donation channel overflow.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card" data-reveal-item>
            <span class="eyebrow">The gap</span>
            <h3>Municipalities need tools that help residents make informed disposal decisions.</h3>
            <p>Sorty was created to close this gap by providing a simple digital tool that helps individuals determine the next best use for their garments, prioritizing reuse, repair, resale, and recycling.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="site-shell section" data-reveal="up">
        <div class="tech-credibility" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--lime);">Technical approach</span>
          <h2>Computer vision meets circular infrastructure.</h2>
          <p>Sorty combines on-device garment classification using computer vision with a condition-assessment questionnaire to generate pathway recommendations. Our AI model is trained on textile categories relevant to North American waste streams, and recommendations are mapped to verified local circular infrastructure — repair shops, consignment stores, donation centres, and textile recyclers. This hybrid approach (AI + structured questions + geospatial data) delivers higher accuracy than a simple lookup database and provides municipalities with anonymized diversion analytics.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="site-shell section" data-reveal="up">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal="up">
          <h2>Decision support for textile circularity</h2>
          <p>Sorty is designed for people getting rid of one shirt and for systems trying to divert thousands of pounds of textile waste.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid three" data-reveal-group>
          <article class="card value-card" data-reveal-item>
            <h3>For residents</h3>
            <p>Understand whether an item is best suited for resale, repair, donation, consignment, or recycling.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card value-card" data-reveal-item>
            <h3>For cities</h3>
            <p>Guide community members toward existing local infrastructure and reduce confusion at the point of disposal.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card value-card" data-reveal-item>
            <h3>For industry</h3>
            <p>Build better data and better pathways for textiles moving through reuse and recovery ecosystems.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

